WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.245
NVIDIA-based Linux AI systems commonly involve the NVIDIA driver,

00:00:04.245 --> 00:00:07.990
CUDA-related runtime libraries, and sometimes a CUDA toolkit.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:12.260
At a high level, the driver enables GPU operation and exposes capabilities to the system.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.020
The CUDA toolkit provides development tools and libraries used to build or run CUDA

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:16.800
applications.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.200
These are related, but they are not the same thing.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.050
nvidia-smi is a common first check because it reports driver information,

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.960
detected NVIDIA GPUs, utilization, memory use, temperature, power,

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.710
and processes using the device.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.780
It is a useful signal,

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.221
but it is not the final proof that a specific AI framework is working.

00:00:33.221 --> 00:00:34.800
A Python library, container,

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.060
or inference runtime may still fail because of missing libraries, incompatible versions,

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.950
or incorrect environment configuration.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.750
Compatibility planning matters.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.200
Driver versions, CUDA runtime libraries, cuDNN and related acceleration libraries,

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.920
Python packages, containers, and inference runtimes may all have version expectations.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.891
Randomly mixing versions can create errors that look like model failures but are really

00:00:55.891 --> 00:00:56.970
stack mismatches.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.505
Stable AI systems benefit from known-good combinations rather than constant chasing of the

00:01:01.505 --> 00:01:02.260
newest packages.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:06.025
GPU visibility should be checked from the places that matter: the host shell,

00:01:06.025 --> 00:01:08.920
Python environment, container, notebook, and inference server.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.620
Each layer can have different visibility and library paths.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:15.630
Document the driver version, runtime versions, container image, model runtime,

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.880
and validation results.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:20.160
That documentation turns a working setup into something recoverable.
